      "observations": [
        "Entry857 passes the persisted interactedWith list from InAppNotifications.getNotifications into NotificationFilter.isActiveNotification and checkProfile. It moves the notification's own-ID exclusion into the filter. Historical checkProfile rejects when ANY displayed_notifications ID occurs in that interaction list; the fixed accepted source rejects when ANY listed ID is absent, so ALL listed IDs are prerequisites. The historical patch and current source have opposite polarity. The later inversion commit and its rationale are outside this audit.",
        "The Bug1918831 description asks for targeting based on previously shown notifications and a record after click, close, or dismissal. Its mutually exclusive donation example is task intent; it does not change the actual historical any-interacted rejection or establish an impression counter. The current markAsInteractedWith deduplicates and schedules persistence, and handleEvent records NotificationManager.NOTIFICATION_INTERACTION_EVENT. Keep the exact serialized displayed_notifications name separate from the local interactedWith naming.",
        "Historical857 returns true for bypassFiltering before checking the notification's interacted ID. The fixed accepted function checks that ID first; its comment gives repeat _tab opening as the reason. Bypass still skips subsequent policy, date, URL, chance, and profile gates. The current bypass assertion covers an invalid date/URL/profile without an interacted ID, and therefore does not directly assert the repeated-ID plus bypass combination.",
        "D222684 was accepted by mkmelin. Both submitted inlines are Done: the checkProfile JSDoc was expanded to cover interaction history, and the reviewer preferred should form in assertion messages so they work in pass and fail cases. The complete retained timeline records a Try link and rebases; it supplies no independently checked test result. Bug1918831 comments0–3 record the landing and ESR uplift through Bug1936307, which was not opened. These outcomes do not make the later current polarity part of the original reviewed patch.",
        "All three historical diffs and all changed tests were read. Added tests directly assert null/empty displayed_notifications match, a listed ID absent from history matches historically, a listed ID present in history rejects historically, and a notification's own interacted ID is inactive. The current two-ID match and one-missing mismatch assertions follow the current opposite polarity. Broad third-argument changes preserve test callers. Nearby guards, callback argument flow, exact wire names, JSDoc, and logical groups were checked statically; no new style rule is inferred."
